    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0148" n="28" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg28"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.6363 Barco/586: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-20T13:00:00-04:00">June 20, 1931—1
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>44. Legation’s 84, June 18, 2 p.m.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d52-f1"/> When the
                    Catatumbo contract has been signed<anchor n="28" xml:id="d52-f2"/> you may, if
                    in your opinion such action would be helpful and would not be misconstrued,
                    express informally to President Olaya the gratification with which this
                    Government has learned of the final satisfactory solution of this troublesome
                    and longstanding problem.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d52-f1" n="27" xml:id="d52-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f2" n="28" xml:id="d52-f2-content">
                <p>President Olaya signed the bill approving the Catatumbo contract on June 20, 1931
                    (821.6363 Barco/592).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
